# What ships in the .vsix — an ALLOWLIST, not a denylist.
#
# vsce packages everything this file does not exclude, so the usual
# "list the junk" form fails open: every new top-level directory (CI config,
# coverage output, agent scratch notes) silently joins the published artifact.
# This repo shipped 140 such files before this was inverted.
#
# So: exclude everything, then re-include only what users need. Adding a
# genuinely shippable path means adding a `!` line here AND to ALLOWED in
# scripts/check-vsix-contents.mjs, which enforces this from the other side and
# runs in CI.
**

# The bundles esbuild produces (extension host + webview) — the actual payload.
!dist/**
!media/**

# Runtime assets: walkthrough media, icons.
!resources/**
!icon.png

# The manifest, and the docs the Marketplace / Open VSX listing renders.
!package.json
!README.md
!CHANGELOG.md
!LICENSE
!SECURITY.md

# Source maps are large and reference paths that do not exist in the .vsix.
**/*.map
